# Skill Evolution & Update Engine

Phase: 136 (spec adopted 2026-09-14; runtime in sdd-adapter)
Owns: skills/evolution.sdd
Command: /sdd-evolve (knowledge evolution; /sdd-update stays git-sync)

Principle: .sdd is not a self-refreshing knowledge repo; it is an
EVOLUTION SYSTEM — it researches, compares, validates, improves, and
SAFELY DELIVERS its knowledge (DISCOVER / EVOLVE / DELIVER separated).

## Pipeline (/sdd-evolve)

```
LOAD SDD + SKILL INDEX (+version/timestamps)
  -> CHECK MAIN REPO (upstream .sdd changes)
  -> DISCOVER NEW KNOWLEDGE (web/official docs, RIE references/)
  -> COMPARE current vs new (per skill due for review)
  -> VALIDATE (source hierarchy, evidence, project fit)
  -> DEDUPLICATE (canonical selection, aliases)
  -> EVOLVE: PROMOTE | UPDATE (incremental v->v+1) | DEPRECATE | ADD
  -> SDD CONSISTENCY CHECK + SKILL TESTS
  -> GENERATE CHANGESET (Update Manifest UPD-<n>)
  -> DELIVER: own repo -> commit/push | other user -> branch+PR
```

## UPDATE != GIT PULL

/sdd-update = git state sync (UPD-01..05 rules, unchanged).
/sdd-evolve = knowledge evolution (this spec). Never conflated.

## Source hierarchy (confidence)

L0 official spec/docs > L1 official repo > L2 maintainer docs >
L3 high-quality engineering sources > L4 community > L5 AI inference.
Every skill change records source level; L5-only changes are
proposals, never direct updates.

## SKILL_EVOLUTION record

```
skill: @<domain>/<name>
status: update_required | new_concept | promotion_candidate |
  dedup_candidate | deprecated
reason: <e.g. current guidance is outdated>
evidence: [L0 doc link, project examples, RIE REF-<n>]
change: <incremental delta description>
confidence: high | medium | low
```

## Skill lifecycle

DISCOVERED -> DRAFT -> VALIDATED -> ACTIVE -> OUTDATED -> EVOLVING
-> ACTIVE; branch: OUTDATED -> DEPRECATED -> REMOVED.
(Removal follows [SK6] marketplace lifecycle; supersession over
deletion — record what replaced it.)

## Skill metadata (mandatory)

```
version: <n>
status: active | draft | outdated | evolving | deprecated
sources: [<provenance>]
last_verified: <date>
review_after: <date>
confidence: high | medium | low
depends_on: [@skill.x, @skill.y]
recommended_for: L0..L5 (project scale — best practice is
  context-dependent: enterprise K8s pattern ≠ small-VPS answer)
```

last_verified + review_after throttle research: only due skills are
re-researched on /sdd-evolve. --deep forces all critical skills;
/sdd-evolve @<domain> scopes to one domain.

## New concept placement

NEW_CONCEPT -> existing parent? -> child skill (parent: @go/concurrency
-> @go/structured-concurrency, status: candidate -> ACTIVE on
validation). Fully new domain -> new skill. Dedup FIRST: near-duplicate
(@ddd/aggregate ~ @domain/aggregate) -> canonical chosen (@ddd/
aggregate-boundary), others become alias/reference/deprecated.

## Knowledge promotion

@project/<pattern> used across 5 projects -> PROMOTION_CANDIDATE ->
@shared/<pattern> proposal. Mirrors marketplace CANDIDATE->ACTIVE
packet flow (promotion-packet.sdd).

## Delivery

Update Manifest: .sdd/updates/UPD-<n> (machine-readable: trigger,
counts, changed skills, sources, validation, delivery mode).
Modes: direct (own repo: update->test->commit->push) |
pull_request (non-collaborator: branch sdd/update/<area>/<slug> ->
commit sdd(skill): update <area> <slug> -> PR). TRUST_0..TRUST_5 gates
map to authority levels L0-L4 + Phase 131 interrupt model (research
only / proposals / local modify / branch+commit / PR / direct push).

PR standard:
```
sdd(skill): update Go concurrency guidance

## Why / ## Changes / ## Sources / ## Validation / ## Risk
```
Every knowledge change carries SOURCE, EVIDENCE, REASON, CHANGE —
"AI bunu haradan uydurdu?" is always answerable.

## Final report

```
SDD EVOLVE COMPLETE
Sources checked / Skills checked / unchanged / updated / new /
deprecated / references added / architecture rules changed / PR link
```

## Research records

.sdd/research/<year>/<topic>.sdd — question, sources, findings,
decision ONLY (no raw web data; RIE tmp snapshots stay tmp, [R96]).
NO_VALUE outcome -> DISCARD is a first-class path (research does not
obligate skill creation).

State: +
